  {
    "id": "comment-guide-en",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "tab-shelly-admin-03-en",
    "name": "Guide / safety",
    "info": "QUICK START\n1. Select only authorized target networks and a localfilesystem Context store in the config node.\n2. Deploy. Use Inject nodes or editor Start/Cancel controls.\n3. Dashboard: http://<node-red-host>:1880/shelly-admin-dashboard-en\n4. Firmware check is read-only. Update dry-run changes nothing.\n5. The real-update path is constrained to a placeholder device ID and also requires explicit arming.\nLifecycle: started/running/cancel-requested/cancelled/completed/completed-with-issues/failed.\nMonitor editor: Settings, Current Findings, History and Device Details are real clickable views. Each read-only result view loads once on first tab selection and then only through its visible Refresh button; there is no periodic editor refresh. Permission-protected Admin endpoints show loading, error and empty states. Structured monitor outputs include summaryText, summaryTextDe, humanSummary, findingsSummary and category cards. Firmware updates first check all selected devices, then plan/update only policy-eligible devices; dry-run exposes plannedUpdates without stagger or validation waits.\nMaintenance editor: Settings, Current Status, Device Overview and History are clickable views. Device Overview shows policy-aware firmware eligibility, check/update results, errors/timeouts and recovery, with Update available, Error, Offline, Successfully updated and Skipped filters.",
    "x": 180,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
